# UI translations (apps + websites)

Canonical: `docs/DEV.md` § Languages · `docs/WEBSITES.md` § Language catalogue.

## Product floor (all Gotigin brands)

Every **app and website** (Kumkaj, Wadhu, Ghal Bol, Gotigin company site)
supports the full language catalogue (**115+ languages**) and **199
countries**. No subset picker. No catalogue language shown without a pack.
No “English-only site” exception for marketing/account chrome.

## Rule

- English source = `en()` in that product’s `src/locale.rs` only.
- Every other catalogue language = `translations/<code>.tsv` (one `key<TAB>text` per `en` key, `{placeholders}` kept).
- **Never** add a user-visible label only in English. After editing `en()`, update **all** packs for that product.
- No shared i18n crate — duplicate the workflow per app/site (copy-then-diverge).
- Sites: packs stage to `/i18n/<code>.tsv`; `lang-nav.js` writes `#l=`; wasm + `site-i18n.js` must repaint. Preference-only pickers are forbidden.

## When you add or change a string

```bash
# after editing apps/<app>/src/locale.rs en()
./scripts/scaffold-ui-translations.sh --app <app> --standin-english
# replace English stand-ins in apps/<app>/translations/*.tsv (agent / manual)
./scripts/check-ui-translations.sh --app <app>
```

Sites: `./scripts/scaffold-ui-translations.sh --site <site>` then
`./scripts/check-ui-translations.sh --site <site>`. Prefer bash (or a
Rust tool) — **no Python** for this workflow (see `no-python-scripts.mdc`).
`cargo test -p <crate> --lib every_catalogue_language_translates_every_key`
must stay green.

## Do not

- Reintroduce `locale_chrome.rs` or a “29 language” subset that leaves catalogue entries in English.
- Ship with `KUMKAJ_ALLOW_TRANSLATION_GAPS=1` (fill-pipeline only).
- Copy TSV packs between apps — each app’s `en()` key set differs.
- Deploy Hosting with a language chip that does not change visible copy.
